@prefix ga:     <https://tesseractsemantics.com/ns/asset-passport/ga#> .
@prefix game:   <https://tesseractsemantics.com/ns/asset-passport/game/> .
@prefix bridge: <https://tesseractsemantics.com/ns/asset-passport/bridge/> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Row of the "Unit mappings" table in rehan-remade/universal-modder,
# knowledge/techniques/bridge-contracts-ownership-units-and-lifecycle.md at
# commit 2131b2cc9e06dac51ebcd202745c03cf3b988ee8. Each number below is the
# row's own; nothing is added that the row does not state.

bridge:um-gta-v-example a ga:Bridge ; rdfs:label "Minecraft x GTA V example (table row)" ;
    ga:host game:gta-v ; ga:guest game:minecraft ;
    ga:declaredMetresPerGuestUnit 1 ; ga:declaredHostUnitsPerGuestUnit 1 ;
    ga:guestXFrom "+x" ; ga:guestYFrom "+z" ; ga:guestZFrom "-y" ;
    ga:evidenceLevel "creator report" ;
    ga:tableRow "| Minecraft × GTA V example | 1 GTA metre = 1 block; GTA (x, y, z) → MC (x, z + yOffset, −y); yaw = 180 − heading |" ;
    ga:note "The row's '1 GTA metre = 1 block' is modelled twice. As written, 1 m per block, it is a claim about Minecraft's block only. Its coordinate map copies GTA's x, y and z into Minecraft without scaling, which also makes it 1 GTA unit per block, a claim that needs GTA V's own unit length. The yOffset and the yaw formula are outside this checker. The row links no project." .
